WEBVTT

00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.231
Prices doubled in under a day.

00:00:02.241 --> 00:00:05.721
Hungary, 1946, just after the Second World

00:00:05.731 --> 00:00:06.029
War:

00:00:06.039 --> 00:00:09.679
the worst hyperinflation ever recorded.

00:00:09.779 --> 00:00:12.938
Its last pengo notes, in July 1946,

00:00:12.948 --> 00:00:16.225
were worth 100 quintillion pengo:

00:00:16.235 --> 00:00:18.146
a one with 20 zeros.

00:00:18.246 --> 00:00:19.436
And it got worse:

00:00:19.446 --> 00:00:21.743
at the peak, prices rose by more

00:00:21.753 --> 00:00:24.486
than 200 percent every single day.

00:00:24.599 --> 00:00:26.064
So how do you fix money that

00:00:26.074 --> 00:00:27.250
is this broken?

00:00:27.260 --> 00:00:27.924
The fix:

00:00:27.934 --> 00:00:29.272
a new currency.

00:00:29.282 --> 00:00:32.868
One forint was worth 400 octillion old

00:00:32.878 --> 00:00:36.061
pengo, wiping out 29 zeros at once.
